  "invariants": [
    "Each Session administers exactly one immutable CaseVersion and has one pinned administration policy.",
    "One attempt contains at most three Sessions and no Session has more than ten minutes of recorded answer.",
    "A Response original, Transcript, ScoringRun and ScoreReport have distinct identities and versions.",
    "Every ScoringRun pins CaseVersion, Response original, Transcript if used, Rubric and scorer configuration.",
    "A Report declares feedback or employer purpose; a purpose change requires a new governed use and participant rights check.",
    "A TargetOutcome is independent of the assessment score and selection decision.",
    "CriterionRating states NA for not fairly elicited and UNK for unusable evidence; neither is zero.",
    "CalibrationSet and ValidationHoldout have disjoint tuning and locked-evaluation uses.",
    "A DecisionThreshold has no employment effect without an authorized DecisionPolicy for the exact context.",
    "Research Evidence does not promote a ClaimTier or authorize hiring use without an exact OwnerDecision.",
    "Public materials never contain unconsented participant source recordings, transcripts or identifying score rows.",
    "A PurposeChoice records a participant action; only a purpose with consent as its approved lawful basis creates a ConsentRecord.",
    "A Challenge, StudyProtocol and Invitation do not confer participant-collection authority without the exact owner and privacy decisions.",
    "An AssessmentAttempt groups up to three SessionAssignments; each assignment pins one case and policy before its Session starts.",
    "A MediaObject, ASRRun, Transcript, TranscriptCorrection, EvidenceSpan, CriterionRating and Adjudication retain distinct identities and lineage.",
    "ResearchExport eligibility is checked against current purpose and withdrawal state at export and downstream access.",
    "A RightsRequest and an AuditEvent are records of requests or actions, not proof that deletion or other downstream work completed.",
    "A CaseCandidate cannot be assigned to a scored Session; only a released immutable CaseVersion can.",
    "GenerationRun, SimilarityAssessment, CaseTrial, CaseEvaluation, CaseReview and CaseDisposition are separate records with separate owners and evidence.",
    "A CaseDisposition can retire a CaseVersion for new assignment without altering historical Response and ScoringRun inputs.",
    "Actor classification, Principal identity, Role, Role Assignment, application Access Permission and Lab Authority remain distinct.",
    "An AccessDecision receipt evaluates one action under a pinned AccessPolicy and cannot supply missing owner authority.",
    "An ExceptionGrant is purpose-, object-, action- and time-bounded and never enables employer use in the MVP.",
    "A product participant or service is not automatically a Lab Actor; any concrete Lab classification and active Role Assignment require their own records and scope."
  ]
